# Scoped licenses for the reproducibility materials

Copyright 2026 Yunya Lin.

The author-approved file scope is recorded in manifests/license_scope.csv: MIT applies to its 37 original Python research/release/test/helper files, including their code comments and docstrings; CC BY 4.0 applies to its 79 original non-text output/identifier/configuration/provenance/documentation files. These are per-file assignments, not alternative licenses for the same material. The previous-candidate SHA256 values preserve the reviewed identities; they are not checksums for later edited metadata. The current export manifest supplies release checksums after final metadata is frozen.

The author's original wording/compilation in this LICENSE, manifests/license_scope.csv, docs/license_scope_policy.md and .zenodo.json is also under CC BY 4.0, as release documentation within the approved scope. Standard license texts retain their own terms. The explicit new-file policy is in docs/license_scope_policy.md; this notice does not automatically license arbitrary future files.

